WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Lightsabers in "Star Wars" are a dime&nbsp;
a dozen – but these particular laser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.940
swords tucked into the background of&nbsp;
Ahsoka's ship may have caught your eye.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.800
While watching Episode 3 of "Ahsoka," a&nbsp;
few eagle-eyed "Star Wars" fans may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.880
spotted a lightsaber collection that&nbsp;
would put General Grievous to shame.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.510
"They are quite elegant, with&nbsp;
several classic design motifs."

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:25.860
The episode&nbsp;&nbsp; opens in the training room&nbsp;
on Ahsoka Tano's starship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.218
where she and Padawan Sabine Wren&nbsp;
enjoy a brief sparring match.

00:00:30.218 --> 00:00:35.160
In the background is an armory packed with a&nbsp;
wide assortment of lightsabers, though oddly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.620
neither Ahsoka nor Sabine ever mentions this&nbsp;
collection. Plenty of fans online are no doubt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.300
wondering who these weapons belonged to before&nbsp;
they wound up on Ahsoka's ship. Presumably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.800
a few of them, or possibly all of them,&nbsp;
were constructed by Huyang, since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.000
ancient droid aided several generations&nbsp;
of Padawans in lightsaber construction.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.900
We know the lightsabers at the top of&nbsp;
the collection are Huyang's work since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:02.040
he carries four identical sabers during&nbsp;
his training session with Sabine — each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.480
sporting a distinctive circle crossguard&nbsp;
and emitting an abnormally thick blade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.920
for practice. While these lightsabers are&nbsp;
clearly for training only, it's worth noting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.020
they all bear a striking resemblance to the&nbsp;
lightsaber of "Star Wars Rebels" staple Kanan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:21.198
Jarrus. which also featured a unique circle&nbsp;
crossguard but emitted a blue beam instead.

00:01:21.198 --> 00:01:24.840
Far more interesting than the practice&nbsp;
sabers are the more distinctive blades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.160
adorning the training facility's back&nbsp;
wall. Each has an extremely unique design,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:33.480
which implies that they belonged to other&nbsp;
Jedi before they wound up in Ahsoka's armory.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.680
While none of these lightsabers immediately&nbsp;
jump out as belonging to any known Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.360
there are a few familiar characteristics&nbsp;
among them. The top right saber and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.640
leftmost saber on the second row sport a sleeve&nbsp;
of black rings, which is an iconic design on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.680
Obi-Wan Kenobi's and Qui-Gon Jinn's weapons in&nbsp;
"The Phantom Menace." The middle right saber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.360
bears a sleeve with black, blocky protrusions&nbsp;
like the lightsabers of Yoda and Mace Windu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.320
while the bottom right saber draws&nbsp;
comparisons to blades of Saesee Tiin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.598
and Darth Vader — both of which have&nbsp;
large, protruding activation switches.

00:02:05.598 --> 00:02:09.780
The most unique of all these sabers&nbsp;
are the two on the top row. The top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.980
left lightsaber sports a thick black&nbsp;
sleeve not unlike Vader's, though oddly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.780
it opens up halfway up the hilt — like a mouth&nbsp;
from which the rest of the blade emerges. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.280
top right weapon is also strange, with&nbsp;
an enormous emitter that juts out above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.840
the blade and seemingly has a chunk cut out.&nbsp;
The overall effect is a group of lightsabers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.981
that look slightly familiar but have not been&nbsp;
connected to any known Jedi, at least not yet.

00:02:32.981 --> 00:02:38.040
Unless Ahsoka or Huyang go out of their way to&nbsp;
identify who originally owned these lightsabers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:42.703
viewers can only speculate on who they might&nbsp;
have belonged to before the show's events.

00:02:42.703 --> 00:02:47.100
If Huyang did not create these lightsabers,&nbsp;
the most likely option is that they belonged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:52.260
to Jedi that escaped the massacre of Order 66.&nbsp;
Ahsoka could have encountered these survivors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:56.640
at any point after the Clone Wars, though if&nbsp;
this is the case, it begs the question of why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.840
she took their lightsabers for her own. More&nbsp;
probable is that they were in the possession&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.684
of non-Jedi who either stole them or found&nbsp;
them after a fallen Jedi cast them aside.

00:03:05.684 --> 00:03:07.484
"Next time, try not to lose it."

00:03:07.742 --> 00:03:08.778
"Yes, master."

00:03:08.778 --> 00:03:10.244
"This weapon is your life."

00:03:10.244 --> 00:03:14.400
In the event that Huyang did construct all these&nbsp;
lightsabers, they were probably made in case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.740
Ahsoka took on another Padawan. If Ahsoka ever&nbsp;
planned to teach other Force wielders the ways of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:24.480
the Jedi, something she almost agreed to do for&nbsp;
Grogu in "The Mandalorian," it stands to reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.580
those new Jedi would need lightsabers. If this is&nbsp;
the case, it's somewhat unfortunate that Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:34.977
brought on Sabine Wren as an apprentice, as she&nbsp;
already has a lightsaber courtesy of Ezra Bridger.

00:03:34.977 --> 00:03:39.720
Regardless, Ahsoka and company clearly have a&nbsp;
huge number of lightsabers at their disposal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:45.540
and one has to wonder if these extra blades will&nbsp;
come in handy as the "Ahsoka" story moves forward.

